                "html": "<h4>The bluestriped fangblenny</h4>\n<p>Dr Karen Cheney studies the bluestriped fangblenny on [[24]] off Queensland's coast. She found that the fangblenny was able to make itself resemble other fish by adjusting its colouration. The fangblenny impersonates the striped cleaner wrasse, a fish that is welcomed by other species as it gets rid of their [[25]]. The fangblenny can approach its [[26]] without drawing the attention of predators or disturbing the work of the striped cleaner wrasse.</p>"
